$b['A human skull appears to have consumed an entire drawing session. Dozens of failed skulls surround and pass through one another. Different jaw positions eye sockets cranial shapes and perspective attempts accumulate into a dense cloud until one final skull emerges in brutally confident black. The previous attempts must remain readable enough that the viewer can reconstruct how the final form was discovered'] = 'The tattoo: A human skull appears to have consumed an entire drawing session. Dozens of failed skulls surround and pass through one another. Different jaw positions, eye sockets, cranial shapes and perspective attempts accumulate into a dense cloud until one final skull emerges in brutally confident black. The previous attempts must remain readable enough that the viewer can reconstruct how the final form was discovered. Obsessive, macabre, masterful. Create exceptional contemporary Sketch tattoo artwork where the visible drawing process is the defining visual language. THE DRAWING PROCESS IS THE STYLE. THE DRAWING LOOKS UNFINISHED. THE ARTWORK IS COMPLETELY INTENTIONAL. Do not create a polished tattoo and surround it with random scratches. Do not create ordinary Fine Line artwork with meaningless loose marks. Every unfinished mark must have a visual reason to exist. Use searching contours, repeated attempts, gesture lines, anatomical construction, centerlines, perspective guides, circles, ellipses, proportion marks, abandoned positions, overshooting strokes, hatching, cross-hatching, scribble shading, charcoal-like darkness, broken contours and selective areas of confident finished drawing. SOME LINES SEARCH. SOME LINES MEASURE. SOME LINES MOVE. SOME LINES COMMIT. Allow the viewer to understand how the artist discovered the final image. Use hierarchy. Not every mark should have equal strength. Preliminary construction can be lighter. Corrections can become more assertive. Final committed areas can use darker confident black. Allow some areas to remain al